**Standard Solution's Key Approach:**
1. Proves a lemma: any triangle with vertices of both colors has all interior point colorings being "good" (by induction).
2. Shows hull vertices of one color must be consecutive (non-interleaving) — giving 2011·2010 + 2 valid hull colorings.
3. **Crucially shows that ANY coloring of the 2011 internal points works** — using the triangle lemma to handle internal points regardless of their colors.
